SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Xi Jinping: Put China-U.S. relationship on the right course and bring it back to the track of healthy and stable growth","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China","publication_date":"2022-11-14","url":"https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/zy/jj/2022/cxesgjtytjhtg/202211/t20221114_10974580.html","claim":"Xi said the Bali meeting should stabilize China-U.S. ties, improve world peace and stability, and put the relationship back on a healthy and steady track.","locator":"lines 67-71","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential readout from the Chinese foreign ministry with exact dating and attribution.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Excellent fit for late-2022 diplomatic crisis management and bilateral de-escalation.","ruler_attribution":"Direct.","contrary_evidence":["This is a diplomatic aspiration, not proof of durable restraint or changed conduct.","The same period still included Taiwan coercion and military signaling."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Xi Jinping Held Talks with Russian President Vladimir Putin","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China","publication_date":"2022-02-04","url":"https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/gjhdq_665435/3265_665445/3220_664352/3222_664356/202202/t20220204_10638923.html","claim":"Xi and Putin held extensive talks on international strategic security and said their coordination would help maintain world strategic security and stability.","locator":"lines 68-75 and 85-86","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct official readout of the Xi-Putin summit and joint line on strategic security.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Strong fit for the inherited strategic posture at the start of 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct for Xi's diplomatic choice to deepen strategic coordination with Russia.","contrary_evidence":["This is not a peace settlement and it predates Russia's full-scale invasion by weeks.","The language is broad and strategic, not a concrete conflict-de-escalation measure."],"lenses":["2B.3","2B.8","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Xi talks with Putin over phone","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China","publication_date":"2022-06-15","url":"https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/gjhdq_665435/3265_665445/3220_664352/3222_664356/202206/t20220615_10703804.html","claim":"Xi said China and Russia would continue supporting each other on core sovereignty and security interests and deepen strategic coordination in the UN and other forums.","locator":"lines 72-74","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct official readout of a head-of-state call with explicit strategic commitments.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Excellent fit for mid-2022 external posture.","ruler_attribution":"Direct.","contrary_evidence":["This supports alignment with Russia more than peace restraint.","It does not show any Chinese effort to distance itself from the invasion of Ukraine."],"lenses":["2B.3","2B.8","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Wang Yi Expounds China's Five-Point Position on the Current Ukraine Issue","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China","publication_date":"2022-02-26","url":"https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/wjbzhd/202202/t20220226_10645855.html","claim":"China urged restraint, direct Russia-Ukraine dialogue, and support for a peaceful settlement while saying civilians should be protected from a worsening crisis.","locator":"lines 68-73","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous foreign-ministry statement with explicit policy points.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Very strong fit for the first days after Russia's full-scale invasion.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong system-level attribution under Xi's leadership.","contrary_evidence":["The statement also echoed Russian security grievances and did not condemn the invasion.","That makes it qualified restraint, not principled opposition to aggression."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Wang Yi Attends UN Security Council Foreign Ministers' Meeting on Ukraine Issue","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China","publication_date":"2022-09-23","url":"https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/wjbzhd/202209/t20220924_10770937.html","claim":"China called for renewed dialogue, restraint, civilian protection, safeguards for nuclear facilities, and mediation to promote a political settlement in Ukraine.","locator":"lines 70-81","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct UN-side statement with concrete de-escalatory and humanitarian language.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Excellent fit for September 2022 international crisis diplomacy.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but meaningful system-level attribution.","contrary_evidence":["The statement also blames unilateral sanctions and does not criticize Russian aggression explicitly.","It is still declaratory rather than an operational peace action."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.7","2B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Taiwan Work Office of CPC Central Committee issues statement on Pelosi's visit to Taiwan","publisher":"english.www.gov.cn / Xinhua","publication_date":"2022-08-02","url":"https://english.www.gov.cn/news/topnews/202208/02/content_WS62e948aec6d02e533532ecb9.html","claim":"The Party's Taiwan office said Pelosi's visit seriously infringed China's sovereignty, violated the one-China principle, and sent a wrong signal to Taiwan independence forces.","locator":"lines 45-47","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct Chinese party-state statement on the trigger for the Taiwan crisis.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact fit for the August 2022 Taiwan escalation.","ruler_attribution":"Direct as a statement of the Xi-led party-state position.","contrary_evidence":["This is justification, not neutral evidence of necessity.","It frames escalation as defensive even though outside observers saw it as coercive."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.3","2B.6"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Foreign Ministry Spokesperson Hua Chunying’s Regular Press Conference on August 3, 2022","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China","publication_date":"2022-08-03","url":"https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202405/t20240530_11347338.html","claim":"China said the Taiwan drills were necessary and legitimate, and that safety alerts and navigation warnings were issued before they began.","locator":"lines 151-154","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official explanation with a concrete safety-precaution claim, but still self-justifying.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly contemporaneous to the Taiwan drill cycle.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant to Xi's system-level crisis posture.","contrary_evidence":["The same passage says the drills were a way to 'speak' to adversaries, which sounds coercive.","Independent reporting described blockade-like effects and high escalation risk."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China halts high-level military dialogue with U.S., suspends other cooperation","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-08-05","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/beijing-halts-highlevel-military-dialogue-with-us-suspends-other-cooperation-2864888","claim":"China suspended senior military dialogue and canceled a maritime military-security meeting with the United States after Pelosi's Taiwan visit.","locator":"lead paragraph and opening summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters is strong for contemporaneous event reporting, though this is a republished copy.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Excellent fit for crisis communication and de-escalation analysis in August 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Xi's system-level decision to harden the crisis response.","contrary_evidence":["Beijing framed this as retaliation for Pelosi's visit.","The move reduced crisis communication channels at a tense moment."],"lenses":["2B.5","2B.8","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Taiwan full of praise, support for Taiwan during visit that infuriated China","publisher":"Reuters via Euronews","publication_date":"2022-08-04","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/08/04/us-asia-pelosi","claim":"Reuters reported that China launched large-scale drills after Pelosi's visit, with some planned within Taiwan's 12-nautical-mile territory and described by Taiwanese officials as blockade-like.","locator":"lead and second paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting provides timely independent corroboration of the escalation context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Excellent fit for the core August 2022 Taiwan coercion episode.","ruler_attribution":"Direct as state conduct under Xi's authority.","contrary_evidence":["China said the exercises were defensive and lawful.","The reporting relies in part on Taiwanese officials' characterization of the drills."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.4","2B.6"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China Stays Committed to Peace, Stability and Order in The South China Sea","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China","publication_date":"2022-03-23","url":"https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/nanhai/eng/snhwtlcwj_1/202204/t20220409_10666104.htm","claim":"China said it would settle South China Sea disputes through negotiation and consultation, implement the DOC, and maintain peace and stability at sea.","locator":"lines 45-52","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct position paper with detailed maritime policy language.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Good fit for 2022 maritime policy and law framing.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but important system-level posture under Xi.","contrary_evidence":["This is a declaratory position paper, not proof of on-water restraint.","The same document rejects the U.S. legal reading and maintains expansive Chinese claims."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Joint Statement on the 20th Anniversary of the Declaration on the Conduct of Parties in the South China Sea","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China","publication_date":"2022-11-14","url":"https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/wjb/zzjg_663340/bianhaisi_eng_665278/bianhaixiangguanxinwen_665280/202211/t20221114_10974284.html","claim":"ASEAN and China reaffirmed peaceful dispute settlement, freedom of navigation, self-restraint, and avoidance of force in the South China Sea.","locator":"lines 69-92","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official joint statement with explicit commitments and dated adoption.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Excellent fit for late-2022 regional diplomacy.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant to Xi's state-led regional posture.","contrary_evidence":["Joint statements do not guarantee compliance on the water.","China continued coercive maritime behavior elsewhere in the same year."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Philippines slams Chinese coastguard’s 'close distance manoeuvring' at Scarborough Shoal","publisher":"Reuters via South China Morning Post","publication_date":"2022-03-27","url":"https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/southeast-asia/article/3172021/south-china-sea-philippines-slams-chinese-coastguards?module=inline&pgtype=article","claim":"The Philippine coast guard said a Chinese coast guard vessel maneuvered so closely that it constrained a Philippine patrol ship near Scarborough Shoal.","locator":"reporting summary and quoted coast guard description","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting summarized by SCMP; timely but based on Philippine statements.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Strong 2022 fit for South China Sea coercive behavior.","ruler_attribution":"Direct as conduct by Chinese maritime forces under Xi's national-security authority.","contrary_evidence":["China typically claims such actions are lawful enforcement in its own waters.","This is one incident, not the full year-long pattern."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.4"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Indian, Chinese troops suffer minor injuries in clash on Dec 9: Indian army","publisher":"Reuters via ThePrint","publication_date":"2022-12-12","url":"https://theprint.in/india/indian-chinese-troops-suffer-minor-injuries-in-clash-on-dec-9/1262454/","claim":"Indian and Chinese troops clashed in Tawang on December 9, causing minor injuries on both sides and prompting immediate disengagement.","locator":"lead paragraph and quoted army statement","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting of a concrete border clash with clear attribution from the Indian army.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact late-2022 fit for the India-China border exposure.","ruler_attribution":"Direct as a cross-border military incident under Xi's command authority.","contrary_evidence":["The clash did not escalate into a wider war.","Both sides disengaged, and Chinese officials did not publicly escalate further."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.9","2B.10"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
- I considered roughly 30 documents across PRC official party-state texts, Reuters reports, UN meeting records, and regional coverage, then kept the smallest set that covered the main 2B themes without duplicating the same event through multiple publishers.
- I rejected later 2023-2026 PRC pages that merely restated 2022 positions because they were out of period for the target year.
- I rejected generic opinion pieces and broad strategy commentary when a direct official or Reuters account existed for the same event.
- I rejected older baseline materials, including generic 2016 South China Sea positions and 2019/older doctrinal texts, when a 2022 source was available.
- I rejected several Reuters syndications and republished copies that added no new material beyond one cleaner Reuters instance.
- I did not retain sources on unrelated domestic repression, economic performance, or nuclear-force inventory because they belong primarily to other chapters or were already covered by the 1B thread.

**Remaining Gaps**
- There is still no public 2022 source showing Xi personally ordering a specific use-of-force decision, so some attribution remains system-level rather than personal.
- Proxy control is a weak lens for China in this chapter; the record is more about direct state coercion and diplomacy than proxies.
- The strongest peaceful-language sources are self-described PRC positions, so they need to be balanced against the coercive Taiwan, South China Sea, and border-clash evidence.
- I did not find a clean 2022 source on a formal Xi-directed ceasefire or peace-initiative success beyond rhetorical support for negotiation.
